keel-lnpp-19.0 (6) keel; urgency=low

  * Stable 1, the first stable release (handbook docs/releases/stable-1-plan.md).
    The image is built on the stable track: it reads trixie of
    archive.keellinux.org and not trixie-testing. It carries keel 0.23.55,
    keel-overlay-syncthing 0.1.0 and syncthing 2.1.6+keel1 (decision 0050).
    File replication runs in the cloud modes (keel#221, keel#224, keel#225,
    keel#228).

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sat, 25 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

keel-lnpp-19.0 (5) keel; urgency=low

  * The image carries keel 0.23.42 from trixie-testing. keel diff does
    not count a sender with no client address as a replica
    (Keel-Linux/keel#201). A join does not say that etcd may not run
    when another step failed (Keel-Linux/keel#198).

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0000

keel-lnpp-19.0 (4) keel; urgency=low

  * A preset disables postgresql-common's WAL archival (pg_receivewal@,
    pg_compresswal@). The first boot applies Debian's presets, which
    enable every unit they do not name: pg_receivewal@17-main streamed
    the WAL into /var/backups, and the server read as a primary in keel
    diff on a node with no replica (Keel-Linux/keel#201). Found by the
    release test of 19.0-3; 19.0-3 is not published.
  * The image carries keel 0.23.41 from trixie-testing: etcd forms with
    every member (Keel-Linux/keel#199), and every mesh peer sends a
    keepalive (Keel-Linux/keel#140).

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:19:36 +0000

keel-lnpp-19.0 (3) keel; urgency=low

  * 40lnpp-check revokes CONNECT on keel_check from PUBLIC again. Only
    the page's role connects. keel 0.23.33 reseeds a pair without
    CONNECT on every database (Keel-Linux/keel#183), and this image
    carries a keel that has it.
  * The image carries keel 0.23.39 from trixie-testing. A paired replica
    gets the primary's Anubis key by itself (Keel-Linux/common#56). etcd
    starts at the third join with no drift (Keel-Linux/keel#188), and
    the VIP overlay waits for etcd with no drift (Keel-Linux/keel#106).

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:14:27 +0000

keel-lnpp-19.0 (2) keel; urgency=low

  * 40lnpp-check keeps CONNECT on keel_check for PUBLIC, PostgreSQL's
    default. keel's reseed of a pair asks pg_database_size() of every
    database as the replication role, and the REVOKE made the reseed of
    the replica fail on hw12-br1 ("permission denied for database
    keel_check"). PUBLIC has no privilege on the table.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:50:00 +0000

keel-lnpp-19.0 (1) keel; urgency=low

  * The first recipe of the lnpp layer (handbook decision 0059): Nginx,
    PostgreSQL 17 and Python 3 with gunicorn, a layer on the web layer
    (bt-layer lnpp --parent web). The database half is keel-postgresql's,
    copied: the postgres role without a password in the image, the two
    loopback addresses, firstboot.d/36pgsqlverify. The manifest
    /usr/share/keel/appliances/lnpp.yaml (base web) declares PostgreSQL
    on the mesh port 5432 and the db_password secret, so a spec can name
    appliance lnpp and declare the pair of decision 0054.
  * The check page at /keel-check/: keel_check.py, a WSGI application
    with no framework that gunicorn serves on the unix socket of
    keel-lnpp-check.socket, as the system user keel-check. It reads
    PostgreSQL by peer authentication, with SELECT on one table only, and
    shows the versions, the role of the server and the rows that
    firstboot.d/40lnpp-check writes. Nginx reaches it through
    /etc/nginx/keel-default.d/50-keel-lnpp.conf (keel-web 0.3.0).
  * conf.d/zz-check fails the build on Apache, on a second appliance
    manifest on top, and on a check page that does not start from its
    socket.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000
